PUBLIC CLASS MAIN {
    PUBLIC STATIC VOID MAIN(STRING[] ARGS) {
        INT[][] ARR = NEW INT[][]{{1,2},{3,4},{5,6}};
        ARR = INSERTENTITY(ARR, 7, 1, 1);

        FOR(INT I=0;I<ARR.LENGTH;I++) {
            FOR(INT J=0;J<ARR[I].LENGTH;J++) {
                SYSTEM.OUT.PRINT(ARR[I][J] + " ");
            }
            SYSTEM.OUT.PRINTLN();
        }
     }

     STATIC INT[][] INSERTENTITY(INT[][] ARR, INT ENTITY, INT X, INT Y){
         IF(ARR.LENGTH>X && ARR[0].LENGTH>Y){
             ARR[X][Y] = ENTITY;
         }ELSE{
             SYSTEM.OUT.PRINTLN("INSERTION INDEX OUT OF BOUNDARY");
         }
         RETURN ARR;
     }
}
```

IN THIS CODE, WE FIRST DECLARE AND INITIALIZE THE 2D ARRAY. IN THE `INSERTENTITY` FUNCTION, WE INSERT THE SPECIFIED ENTITY (7) INTO THE GIVEN COORDINATES (1,1) AFTER CHECKING IF THE COORDINATES DO NOT EXCEED THE ARRAY'S DIMENSIONS. THEN, WE PRINT THE ELEMENTS OF THE MODIFIED ARRAY TO THE SCREEN.

PLEASE NOTE THAT 2D ARRAY INDICES IN JAVA START FROM 0, SO THE COORDINATES [1,1] REFER TO THE SECOND ROW AND THE SECOND COLUMN. FOR ARRAY [[1,2],[3,4],[5,6]], THE OUTPUT WILL THEREFORE BE

1 2  
7 4  
5 6

